---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../components/SiteFooter.astro';
import Imprint from '../components/Imprint.astro';
import { COMPANY } from '../lib/company';
import { PLANS } from '../lib/plans';

const user = Astro.locals.user;

/**
 * Fixed, not `new Date()` — this is the date the terms last changed, and a
 * build must not silently restate today as the effective date.
 */
const updated = '11 August 2026';
---

<Base title="Terms of service">
  <div class="page">
    <SiteHeader user={user} />

    <div class="wrap prose-wrap stack gap-20" style="padding-block: 48px 64px">
      <header>
        <h1 class="h2">Terms of service</h1>
        <p class="small muted" style="margin-top: 8px">
          These terms govern your use of Easy Screen Capture at {COMPANY.site}. By creating an account you agree to
          them. Last updated {updated}.
        </p>
      </header>

      <Imprint heading="Who you are contracting with" />

      <section class="stack gap-8">
        <h2 class="h4">1. The service</h2>
        <p class="small muted">
          Easy Screen Capture renders a web page you name and returns image or PDF files of it. Captures can be made
          from the app or, on plans that include it, over the API. Files are stored in your account and reachable
          through links that carry a share token.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="stack gap-8">
        <h2 class="h4">2. Your account</h2>
        <p class="small muted">
          One person or organisation per account. Keep your password and API keys secret — anything captured with your
          key counts against your quota and is treated as your activity. Tell us at once if a key is exposed; you can
          revoke it yourself on the API screen at any time. You must be 18 or older, or have the consent of a parent
          or guardian.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="stack gap-8">
        <h2 class="h4">3. Acceptable use</h2>
        <p class="small muted">Capture pages you are allowed to access. You must not use the service to:</p>
        <ul class="stack gap-6 small muted">
          <li>· bypass paywalls, logins, rate limits or any other access control;</li>
          <li>· harvest personal data, or capture material that is unlawful to hold or distribute;</li>
          <li>· place load on sites you neither own nor have permission to test, or take part in an attack;</li>
          <li>· resell the service as a substantially identical screenshot API of your own;</li>
          <li>· work around plan quotas, for instance by spreading one workload over several accounts.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="small muted">
          Requests to internal, private and loopback addresses are refused by the service itself, and some hosts are
          blocked outright.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="stack gap-8">
        <h2 class="h4">4. Captured content</h2>
        <p class="small muted">
          A capture reproduces someone else's page. You are responsible for having the right to make and use that
          reproduction, and you keep whatever rights you already had in it — we claim none. We store and serve your
          captures solely to run the service for you.
        </p>
        <p class="small muted">
          If you believe a capture stored here infringes your rights or should not be public, write to{' '}
          <a href={`mailto:${COMPANY.email}`}>{COMPANY.email}</a> with the file link and what is wrong. We remove
          material that is unlawful, and we may disable a share link while we look into a report.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="stack gap-8">
        <h2 class="h4">5. Plans, quotas and payment</h2>
        <p class="small muted">
          Each plan includes a monthly allowance of screenshots — {PLANS.free.quota} on {PLANS.free.name},
          {' '}{PLANS.plus.quota.toLocaleString('en-US')} on {PLANS.plus.name},
          {' '}{PLANS.pro.quota.toLocaleString('en-US')} on {PLANS.pro.name} and
          {' '}{PLANS.business.quota.toLocaleString('en-US')} on {PLANS.business.name}. A scroll series counts one
          screenshot per frame. Allowances reset at the start of each calendar month (UTC) and do not carry over.
          Captures made on the {PLANS.free.name} plan carry a small {COMPANY.site} mark.
        </p>
        <p class="small muted">
          Paid plans are billed in advance, monthly or yearly, and renew automatically for the same period until
          cancelled. Prices are shown on the <a href="/pricing">pricing page</a> in US dollars; where VAT or another
          sales tax applies it is worked out at checkout and shown before you pay. Payments are handled by Stripe —
          we never see your card details. If a payment fails we may suspend paid features until it is settled.
        </p>
        <p class="small muted">
          Captures are kept for {PLANS.free.historyDays} days on {PLANS.free.name}, {PLANS.plus.historyDays} days on
          {' '}{PLANS.plus.name} and {PLANS.pro.name}, and {PLANS.business.historyDays} days on
          {' '}{PLANS.business.name}. Older captures and their files are deleted automatically.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="stack gap-8">
        <h2 class="h4">6. Right of withdrawal</h2>
        <p class="small muted">
          As a consumer in the EU you normally have 14 days to withdraw from a distance contract. Because the service
          is digital content supplied at once, checkout asks you to confirm that you want it to start immediately and
          that you understand you lose that right when it does. If you give that confirmation, the 14-day withdrawal
          right does not apply and the fee for the period you bought is not refundable.
        </p>
        <p class="small muted">
          This does not affect your statutory rights if the service is faulty. If it does not work as described, write
          to <a href={`mailto:${COMPANY.email}`}>{COMPANY.email}</a> and we will put it right or refund you.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="stack gap-8">
        <h2 class="h4">7. Changing and cancelling</h2>
        <p class="small muted">
          You can move to a higher plan at any time; Stripe charges the difference for the rest of the current period.
          You can cancel at any time from the billing screen. Cancellation takes effect at the end of the period you
          have already paid for — your plan keeps working until then, and the account drops to {PLANS.free.name}
          {' '}afterwards rather than being deleted.
        </p>
        <p class="small muted">
          We may change prices or what a plan includes. We will tell you by email at least 30 days beforehand, and the
          change takes effect at your next renewal; if you do not want it, cancel before then.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="stack gap-8">
        <h2 class="h4">8. Availability</h2>
        <p class="small muted">
          We work to keep the service up but do not guarantee uninterrupted availability. Rendering depends on
          Cloudflare Browser Rendering, and captures may fail for pages that block automation, require sign-in, or
          take too long to load. A failed capture does not count against your allowance. Maintenance and third-party
          outages happen; extended downtime that we caused is handled under clause 10.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="stack gap-8">
        <h2 class="h4">9. Suspension</h2>
        <p class="small muted">
          We may suspend or close an account that breaks clause 3, that we are required to act on by law, or whose
          payments remain unsettled. Except where the breach is serious or unlawful, we will tell you first and give
          you a chance to fix it. If we close a paying account for a reason other than your breach, we refund the
          unused part of the period.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="stack gap-8">
        <h2 class="h4">10. Liability</h2>
        <p class="small muted">
          The service is provided as it stands. To the extent the law allows, our total liability for any claim
          arising from these terms is limited to what you paid us in the twelve months before it arose, and we are not
          liable for lost profit, lost data or indirect loss. Nothing here limits liability for death or personal
          injury, for intent or gross negligence, or any liability that Bulgarian law does not permit to be limited —
          including your statutory rights as a consumer.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="stack gap-8">
        <h2 class="h4">11. Privacy</h2>
        <p class="small muted">
          What we collect and how long we keep it is set out in the <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a>, which forms
          part of these terms.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="stack gap-8">
        <h2 class="h4">12. Changes to these terms</h2>
        <p class="small muted">
          We may update these terms. Material changes are announced by email at least 30 days in advance and apply
          from your next renewal. Continuing to use the service after they take effect means you accept them.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="stack gap-8">
        <h2 class="h4">13. Law and disputes</h2>
        <p class="small muted">
          Bulgarian law governs these terms, and the courts of Sofia, Bulgaria have jurisdiction. If you are a
          consumer, this does not deprive you of the protection of the mandatory law of the country you live in, and
          you may also bring a claim in your own courts. The European Commission's online dispute resolution platform
          is at <a href="https://ec.europa.eu/consumers/odr" rel="noopener">ec.europa.eu/consumers/odr</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="stack gap-8">
        <h2 class="h4">14. Contact</h2>
        <p class="small muted">
          {COMPANY.name}, {COMPANY.address.street}, {COMPANY.address.postcode} {COMPANY.address.city},
          {' '}{COMPANY.address.country} · <a href={`mailto:${COMPANY.email}`}>{COMPANY.email}</a>
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>

    <SiteFooter />
  </div>
</Base>
